# Skia Color Picker — a blurred sweep-gradient + runtime-shader HSV wheel with a pin-shaped picker; the picker follows the finger (clamped to the wheel) and is filled with the rgba() computed from hue/saturation in a worklet.
# What this test covers: tap-to-jump at several hues (onBegin moves the pin), the exact centre (saturation 0, grey
# branch of hsvToRgb), drags far outside the wheel (clamped to the rim, saturation ~100), a sweep around the rim
# through every hue sector, crossing the centre, a fast fling across the canvas, and a pan in the canvas corner.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/skia-color-picker"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 1500
# Tap-to-jump around the wheel.
press 300 377
wait 400
press 120 500
wait 400
press 201 330
wait 400
press 260 520
wait 400
# Exact centre: saturation 0.
press 201 437
wait 500
# Drag well outside the wheel: clamped to the rim.
gesture pan 201 437 190 0 500
wait 400
gesture pan 380 437 0 -190 500
wait 400
# Sweep the rim through every hue sector (each pan is clamped to the circle).
gesture pan 343 437 -142 -142 400
gesture pan 201 295 -142 142 400
gesture pan 59 437 142 142 400
gesture pan 201 579 142 -142 400
wait 500
# Cross the centre from one side of the rim to the other.
gesture pan 80 330 240 220 800
wait 400
# Fast fling across the canvas.
gesture pan 30 260 340 360 120
wait 500
# A pan starting in the canvas corner (outside the wheel).
gesture pan 15 250 60 60 400
wait 800
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
